{"operations":[{"content":"def median(data):\n    \"\"\"Return the median of the data as a float.\n\n    For an even number of values, the median is the arithmetic mean of the two middle values.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_data = sorted(data)\n    n = len(sorted_data)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return float(sorted_data[mid])\n    else:\n        return (float(sorted_data[mid - 1]) + float(sorted_data[mid])) / 2.0\n\ndef mean(data):\n    \"\"\"Return the arithmetic mean of the data as a float.\"\"\"\n    return sum(data) / len(data) if data else 0.0\n","expected_sha256":"d4ebc5391a49a2bcccbe8e83801cc6d8d5d623026591ce17a95053be92810b62","kind":"modify","path":"src/stats.py"}],"rationale":"Added the missing mean function to src/stats.py to fix ImportError in tests. Also ensured median returns float for even number of values by converting operands to float before averaging."}